        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): load real Cron and Skills counts in Quick Settings Automations (#107852)",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nThe Quick Settings (Settings -> Simple) Automations card always showed \"0 scheduled tasks\" and \"0 skills installed\" regardless of the real Gateway state. `cronJobCount` and `skillCount` were hardcoded to `0` in `renderQuickSettings`; only `mcpServerCount` was computed. This loads both inventories from the Gateway (`cron.list` + `skills.status`), mirroring the existing `system.info` loader, and renders real counts, a placeholder while loading/offline, or an unavailable label when the Gateway cannot serve those methods.\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nControl UI Settings -> Simple -> Automations displayed misleading zero counts for scheduled tasks and installed skills even on healthy installations with real cron jobs and skills. Operators could not tell whether the Gateway genuinely had no automations or the counts were simply not loaded, which sent them to troubleshooting/configuration pages unnecessarily (issue #107852).\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\nBefore: `ui/src/pages/config/config-page.ts` built the automation card state as `cronJobCount: 0, skillCount: 0` (hardcoded), so the card could never show a non-zero value.\r\n\r\nAfter: the card loads real counts via `cron.list` (the `total` field) and `skills.status` (`skills.length`), using the same request-id race-guard + gateway-source-binding + unavailable-state pattern as the adjacent `system.info` loader (`loadSystemInfo`). Counts render real values, a `-` placeholder while loading/offline, or an `Unavailable` label when the Gateway cannot serve the methods.\r\n\r\nUnit tests (vitest, Node v22.22.3, jsdom):\r\n- `quick.test.ts`: renders `3 scheduled tasks` / `5 skills installed` / `2 MCP servers` from loaded counts; renders `-` (not `0`) while loading/offline; renders `Unavailable` when the Gateway lacks support.\r\n- `config-page.test.ts`: `supportsQuickAutomation` requires both `cron.list` and `skills.status`; `loadQuickAutomation` derives `{cronJobCount: 3, skillCount: 5}` from the two RPC responses; marks the inventory unavailable when the Gateway lacks support.\r\n\r\n```\r\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\r\n     Tests  48 passed (48)\r\n```\r\n\r\n`tsgo` typecheck (ui prod + ui tests): exit 0, no type errors.\r\n\r\n## Real behavior proof\r\n\r\n- Behavior or issue addressed: #107852 - Quick Settings Automations card hardcodes cron/skill counts to 0.\r\n- Real environment tested: Windows 10, Node v22.22.3, vitest jsdom environment (Control UI is a Lit/browser component; rendered output is asserted through the DOM).\r\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch: `node node_modules/vitest/dist/cli.js run ui/src/pages/config/quick.test.ts ui/src/pages/config/config-page.test.ts --reporter=dot`\r\n- Evidence after fix: vitest reports `2 passed (2) / 48 passed (48)`; new tests assert the rendered Automation rows show real counts (`3 scheduled tasks`, `5 skills installed`), a `-` placeholder before load, and `Unavailable` when the Gateway cannot serve the inventory.\r\n- Observed result after fix: the Automation rows no longer render a misleading `0`; they render the loaded count, a loading placeholder, or an unavailable label.\r\n- What was not tested: a live Gateway + browser session showing the populated card (no live Gateway available in this sandbox).\r\n- Proof limitations or environment constraints: Windows sandbox without a running OpenClaw Gateway; real behavior is covered by unit tests that render the actual `renderQuickSettings` output and exercise the real `loadQuickAutomation` code path with a fake Gateway client, plus `tsgo` type validation.\r\nbefore\r\n<img width=\"840\" height=\"274\" alt=\"beforecount\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ba7e6eba-c4b1-4d8d-8fc2-8911369b3752\" />\r\n<img width=\"1169\" height=\"754\" alt=\"beforecountskill\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95f366b4-f6d6-4d2f-8eb6-cce457b45188\" />\r\nafter\r\n<img width=\"814\" height=\"294\" alt=\"fixcount\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4cdfe5ec-dea6-43a5-80c6-967b4b71d4ac\" />\r\n\r\n## Tests and validation\r\n\r\n- `npx oxlint <changed files>` - clean.\r\n- `vitest run quick.test.ts config-page.test.ts` - 2 files, 48 tests passed.\r\n- `tsgo:ui` and `tsgo:test:ui` - exit 0 (no type errors; `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` satisfied via optional chaining).\r\n\r\nNew/updated tests:\r\n- `quick.test.ts`: three tests covering real counts, loading placeholder, and unavailable label.\r\n- `config-page.test.ts`: `supportsQuickAutomation` unit test + `loadQuickAutomation` loader test (counts + unavailable).\r\n\r\nWhat failed before this fix: the Automation card always rendered `0 scheduled tasks` / `0 skills installed`.\r\n\r\n## Risk checklist\r\n\r\nDid user-visible behavior change? Yes - the Automations card now shows real counts (or a placeholder/unavailable label) instead of a hardcoded 0.\r\n\r\nDid config, environment, or migration behavior change? No.\r\n\r\nDid security, auth, secrets, network, or tool execution behavior change? No (two existing read-only RPCs: `cron.list`, `skills.status`).\r\n\r\nWhat is the highest-risk area? The new `loadQuickAutomation` loader running on the Quick Settings page; it shares the `system.info`-style race-guard pattern so stale Gateway responses are discarded.\r\n\r\nHow is that risk mitigated? request-id race guards, gateway-source binding, an `unavailable` state for unsupported/missing-scope, and the existing `PollController` lifecycle (stopped on disconnect). Counts are read-only; no writes.\r\n\r\n## Current review state\r\n\r\nWhat is the next action? Reviewer approval (UI/UX area).\r\n\r\nWhat is still waiting on author, maintainer, CI, or external proof? CI (`real-behavior-proof`, `check-test-types`, `ci-gate`); a live-Gateway screenshot is not available from this sandbox (covered by unit tests).\r\n\r\nWhich bot or reviewer comments were addressed? None yet (new PR).\r\n\r\n## Linked context\r\n\r\nCloses #107852\r\n",
